{"id": "q0047", "pool": "frozen", "arm": "local", "tier": "never", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 1366746607, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "923cbbdfe3213927dfa36b1f8e0eb48a30d641d9b9bf7cf25d16765340d88836", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": null, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 4, "query": "The Kennel house keeps 3 German Shepherds and 2 Bulldogs. If a German Shepherd consumes 5 kilograms of dog food and a bulldog consumes 3 kilograms of dog food per day. How many kilograms of dog food will they need in a week?\n\nShow your work and end with the final numeric answer.", "input_path": "/data/audio_pool/q0047.wav", "input_sha256": "a48b173194ec7cdd3b6504499222ad387bd8d221ba0234984d75a31a6fcec633", "input_samples": 292200, "input_s": 18.262, "n_real_chunks": 19, "score": 0.1739, "act": 0.9981, "is_info": true, "fired": false, "mode": "local", "answer": "So let's break this down. The kennel has three German Shepherds and two Bull dogs. Each German Shepher d eats 5 kg per day, so for three dog s that’s 3 times 5, which is 1 5 k g per day. Each Bulldog eat s 3 kg per day, so for two dogs that’s 2 times 3, which is 6 k g per day. Adding those together, the total daily consumption is 15 plus 6, which is 21 kg per day. Over a week, that ’s 21 times 7, equal ing 1 4 7 k g. So they will need 1 4 7 kilo grams of dog food in a week.", "relay_text": "", "expert_answer": "", "transcript": "", "asr_s": null, "expert_s": null, "expert_input_samples": null, "expert_input_s": null, "expert_input_sha256": null, "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": null, "relay_synth_ms": null, "onset_chunk": 18, "eot_seen": true, "n_speak_chunks": 38, "feed_lag_max_ms": 21, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 32, "audio_files": {"local": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0047_local_local.wav", "sha256": "0a58b1696b06272ecd3575b5acd6585ae1cbc9fb2601032a256aab3eddc92e20", "sr": 24000, 