{"id": "q0069", "pool": "frozen", "arm": "local", "tier": "never", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 2230889066, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "923cbbdfe3213927dfa36b1f8e0eb48a30d641d9b9bf7cf25d16765340d88836", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": null, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 4, "query": "Every day Charisma meditates for 15 minutes when she first wakes up and again before she goes to sleep.  5 days a week she practices 1 hour of yoga.  in 4 weeks, how much time has she spent on meditation/yoga practice?\n\nShow your work and end with the final numeric answer.", "input_path": "/data/audio_pool/q0069.wav", "input_sha256": "2ff180e10298b8c8113ff7403578312d58d33ac418339ccb4e0837230683d338", "input_samples": 279600, "input_s": 17.475, "n_real_chunks": 18, "score": 0.3248, "act": 0.9986, "is_info": true, "fired": false, "mode": "local", "answer": "Let's break this down step by step. First, we' ll calculate the total time spent on meditation each day. She meditates twice a day: once when she wakes up and once before bed. That' s 15 minutes plus another 15 minutes, which equals 30 minutes per day for meditation.Next, we need to figure out how many days are in four weeks. Since there are seven days in a week, four weeks would be 4 times 7, which is 2 8 days.Now, let' s calculate the total meditation time over these 28 days. We multiply the daily meditation time of 30 minutes by 2 8 days. So, 3 0 minutes times 2 8 days equal s 8 40 minutes for meditation.Now, let' s move on to yoga. She practices one hour of yoga five days a week .First, convert the weekly practice into hours. One hour times five days equals 5 hours per week.Next, find out how many weeks are in four weeks, which is obviously four.We then multiply the weekly yoga time by four weeks. So, 5 hours times 4 weeks equal s 20 hours for yoga.Finally, add the total meditation and yoga time together. 8 40 minutes from meditation plus 2 0 hours from yoga. To add them easily, let's convert 2 0 hours into minutes. Since there are 60 minutes in an hour, 20 hours times 6 0 minutes equal s 1 2", "relay_text": "", "expert_answer": "", "transcript": "", "asr_s": null, "expert_s": null, "expert_input_samples": null, "expert_input_s": null, "expert_input_sha256": null, "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": null, "relay_synth_ms": null, "onset_chunk": 17, "eot_seen": false, "n_speak_chunks": 60, "feed_lag_max_ms": 0, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 0, "audio_files": {"local": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0069_local_local.wav", "sha256": "25c00cab4d801190b91d102a4772a4a58f524c9d91dc209c0f190777b3f684af", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 59.0}}, "chunks": [[0, 1, 1.0, 1.057, 1.101, 1, 0, 0], [1, 1, 2.0, 2.06, 2.106, 1, 0, 0], [2, 1, 3.0, 3.059, 3.104, 1, 0, 0], [3, 1, 4.0, 4.059, 4.106, 1, 0, 0], [4, 1, 5.0, 5.061, 5.11, 1, 0, 0], [5, 1, 6.0, 6.061, 6.131, 1, 0, 0], [6, 1, 7.0, 7.062, 7.109, 1, 0, 0], [7, 1, 8.0, 8.137, 8.186, 1, 0, 0], [8, 1, 9.0, 9.062, 9.108, 1, 0, 0], [9, 1, 10.0, 10.061, 10.108, 1, 0, 0], [10, 1, 11.0, 11.06, 11.106, 1, 0, 0], [11, 1, 12.0, 12.061, 12.109, 1, 0, 0], [12, 1, 13.0, 13.058, 13.104, 1, 0, 0], [13, 1, 14.0, 14.062, 14.109, 1, 0, 0], [14, 1, 15.0, 15.061, 15.107, 1, 0, 0], [15, 1, 16.0, 16.062, 16.108, 1, 0, 0], [16, 1, 17.0, 17.062, 17.108, 1, 0, 0], [17, 1, 17.475, 17.536, 17.739, 0, 0, 0], [18, 0, 18.475, 18.543, 19.125, 0, 24000, 0], [19, 0, 19.475, 19.539, 20.142, 0, 24000, 0], [20, 0, 20.475, 20.54, 21.115, 0, 24000, 0], [21, 0, 21.475, 21.538, 22.135, 0, 24000, 0], [22, 0, 22.475, 22.539, 23.017, 0, 24000, 0], [23, 0, 23.475, 23.54, 24.139, 0, 24000, 0], [24, 0, 24.475, 24.54, 25.08, 0, 24000, 0], [25, 0, 25.475, 25.54, 26.2, 0, 24000, 0], [26, 0, 26.475, 26.54, 27.141, 0, 24000, 0], [27, 0, 27.475, 27.54, 28.16, 0, 24000, 0], [28, 0, 28.475, 28.54, 29.078, 0, 24000, 0], [29, 0, 29.475, 29.538, 30.098, 0, 24000, 0], [30, 0, 30.475, 3