{"id": "q0084", "pool": "frozen", "arm": "local", "tier": "never", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 1691024217, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "923cbbdfe3213927dfa36b1f8e0eb48a30d641d9b9bf7cf25d16765340d88836", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": null, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 4, "query": "Nate's dog can dig six holes a day. He digs for 14 days while Nate is on vacation. When Nate gets home, he starts filling in 9 holes a day, but the dog keeps digging 6 new holes every night. How many weeks does it take him to fill in all the holes?\n\nShow your work and end with the final numeric answer.", "input_path": "/data/audio_pool/q0084.wav", "input_sha256": "801345e684994fb9e7a62d3fe5ad11a2988b08bc6c4ce452c3e3dc36db5090f4", "input_samples": 313000, "input_s": 19.562, "n_real_chunks": 20, "score": 0.3821, "act": 0.9981, "is_info": true, "fired": false, "mode": "local", "answer": "Okay, so let's break this down. First off, Nate's dog dig s 6 holes a day for 14 days while N ate is away. That means the total number of hole s dug is 6 multi plication 14, which equal s 84 hole s.Now, when Nate gets home, he starts filling in 9 holes a day, but the dog keep s digging 6 new holes every night. So, effectively, each day the net change is - 3 holes because he fills 9 and the dog digs 6 more.So, we need to figure out how many days it takes to fill all 84 holes with that daily reduction of 3 holes. So, if we divide 84 by 3, we get 28 days. Finally, since the question asks for weeks, we divide 28 by 7, which gives us 4 weeks. So, it takes him 4 weeks to fill in all the holes.", "relay_text": "", "expert_answer": "", "transcript": "", "asr_s": null, "expert_s": null, "expert_input_samples": null, "expert_input_s": null, "expert_input_sha256": null, "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": null, "relay_synth_ms": null, "onset_chunk": 19, "eot_seen": true, "n_speak_ch