{"id": "q0103", "pool": "frozen", "arm": "local", "tier": "never", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 867536581, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "923cbbdfe3213927dfa36b1f8e0eb48a30d641d9b9bf7cf25d16765340d88836", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": null, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 4, "query": "The data in the table below shows the percent of bus riders in a survey of Central H.S. students; 300 males and 300 females in each grade were surveyed. For which grade is the number of its male bus riders closest to $135\\%$ of the number of its female bus riders? \\begin{tabular}{|l|c|c|}\\hline\nGrade & Males & Females \\\\ \\hline\n$9^{\\mathrm{th}}$ grade & $41.1\\%$ & $39.4\\%$ \\\\ \\hline\n$10^{\\mathrm{th}}$ grade & $34.4\\%$ & $33.1\\%$ \\\\ \\hline\n$11^{\\mathrm{th}}$ grade & $20.6\\%$ & $13.8\\%$ \\\\ \\hline\n$12^{\\mathrm{th}}$ grade & $11.6\\%$ & $8.6\\%$ \\\\ \\hline\n\\end{tabular}\n\nSolve and give the final answer.", "input_path": "/data/audio_pool/q0103.wav", "input_sha256": "adbc6ffc5dc5203fb5bd83ab83bfe8ae216fcd2142658aed2c0feeef3dc61470", "input_samples": 675000, "input_s": 42.188, "n_real_chunks": 43, "score": 0.8442, "act": 0.9998, "is_info": true, "fired": false, "mode": "local", "answer": "So, for each grade, we need to find the number of male bus riders and compare it to 1 35% of the number of female bus rid ers. Let's start with ninth grade. In ninth grade, there are 4 1.1% male bus riders and 39.4% female bus riders. So, if we take 3 9. 4% and multi ply it by 1.3 5, we get about 5 3.7%. But the actual number of male bus rid ers is only 21. 1 %, which is quite a bit lower than 53.7%. Next, let' s look at tenth grade. In tenth grade, there are 1 3.8% male bus riders and 1 1.6% female bus riders. If we take 11.6% and multiply it by 1.3 5, we get about 15. 7%. The actual number of male bus riders is 1 3.8%, which is closer to 1 5