{"id": "q0152", "pool": "frozen", "arm": "local", "tier": "never", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 969230870, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "923cbbdfe3213927dfa36b1f8e0eb48a30d641d9b9bf7cf25d16765340d88836", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": null, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 4, "query": "The value of the coefficient K_G in a wetted wall column forthe absorption of SO_2 in air by water at 70°F is 0.068lbmol/hr \\bulletsqft\\bullet atm.The resistance of gas and liquid filmsare equal in the absorption of SO_2. The diffusivities of SO_2 and NH_3 at 49°F are 0.115 and 0.168 cm^2/sec, respectively. Find the value of for the absorption of NH_3 in waterat 49°F when all other conditions are the same.\n\nA. 0.085lbmol/hr sqft atm\nB. 0.05lbmol/hr sqft atm\nC. 0.188lbmol/hr sqft atm\nD. 0.174lbmol/hr sqft atm\nE. 0.16lbmol/hr sqft atm\nF. 2.428lbmol/hr sqft atm\nG. 0.068lbmol/hr sqft atm\nH. 0.210lbmol/hr sqft atm\nI. 0.135lbmol/hr sqft atm\nJ. 0.092lbmol/hr sqft atm\n\nAnswer with the correct option letter and its content.", "input_path": "/data/audio_pool/q0152.wav", "input_sha256": "5bc334acc43549a5dad6d15216ed7e1ffbcbfbce19b3c814c0341b9020538699", "input_samples": 893400, "input_s": 55.837, "n_real_chunks": 56, "score": 0.9026, "act": 0.9988, "is_info": true, "fired": false, "mode": "local", "answer": "Okay, so we have the value of K G for S O 2 absorption in air by water at 7 0 degrees F as 0. 06 8 pounds-m ole per hour square foot atm. We' re told that the resistance of gas and liquid film s are equal, which means it's a case of equal resistances or control by both sides. The diffus ivities given are for S O 2 and NH 3 at 49 degrees C, 0.1 15 and 0. 16 8 centimeters square per second respectively. Now, since all other conditions are the same except for the solute, we can use the ratio of diffus ivities to estimate the new K G value for N H 3. When the resistance s are equal, K G is proportional to the square root of the di ffusivity. So I need to find the ratio of the diffusivities first. That would be D NH 3 over D S O 2, which is 0. 16 8 divided by 0.1 15. Let me calculate that. That gives me approximately 1. 46. Then I take the square root of that, which is about 1. 21. So", "relay_text": "", "expert_answer": "", "transcript": "", "asr_s": null, "expert_s": null, "expert_input_samples": null, "expert_input_s": null, "expert_input_sha256": null, "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": null, "relay_synth_ms": null, "onset_chunk": 56, "eot_seen": false, "n_speak_chunks": 60, "feed_lag_max_ms": 0, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 0, "audio_files": {"local": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0152_local_local.wav", "sha256": "6ec02ba14409f0811be465893dfbb15d53209c9150c688f65b5a78e5dfe83314", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 60.0}}, "chunks": [[0, 1, 1.0, 1.055, 1.098, 1, 0, 0], [1, 1, 2.0, 2.06, 2.106, 1, 0, 0], [2, 1, 3.0, 3.059, 3.104, 1, 0, 0], [3, 1, 4.0, 4.059, 4.106, 1, 0, 0], [4, 1, 5.0, 5.056, 5.099, 1, 0, 0], [5, 1, 6.0, 6.059, 6.105, 1, 0, 0], [6, 1, 7.0, 7.057, 7.1, 1, 0, 0], [7, 1, 8.0, 8.059, 8.105, 1, 0, 0], [8, 1, 9.0, 9.057, 9.102, 1, 0, 0], [9, 1, 10.0, 10.059, 10.105, 1, 0, 0], [10, 1, 11.0, 11.059, 11.104, 1, 0, 0], [11, 1, 12.0, 12.062, 12.108, 1, 0, 0], [12, 1, 13.0, 13.059, 13.103, 1, 0, 0], [13, 1, 14.0, 14.06, 14.105, 1, 0, 0], [14, 1, 15.0, 15.061, 15.105, 1, 0, 0], [15, 1, 16.0, 16.063, 16.108, 1, 0, 0], [16, 1, 17.0, 17.059, 17.102, 1, 0, 0], [17, 1, 18.0, 18.063, 18.109, 1, 0, 0], [18, 1, 19.0, 19.064, 19.111, 1, 0, 0], [19, 1, 20.0, 20.065, 20.112, 1, 0, 0], [20, 1, 21.0, 21.063, 21.109, 1, 0, 0], [21, 1, 22.0, 22.064, 22.11, 1, 0, 0], [22, 1, 23.0, 23.064, 23.11, 1, 0, 0], [23, 1, 24.0, 24.064, 24.11, 1, 0, 0], [24, 1, 25.0, 25.062, 25.107, 1, 0, 0], [25, 1, 26.0, 26.066, 26.113, 1, 0, 0], [26, 1, 27.0, 27.064, 27.11, 1, 0, 0], [27, 1, 28.0, 28.066, 28.113, 1, 0, 0], [28, 1, 29.0, 29.064, 29.