{"id": "q0175", "pool": "frozen", "arm": "local", "tier": "never", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 2509749559, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "923cbbdfe3213927dfa36b1f8e0eb48a30d641d9b9bf7cf25d16765340d88836", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": null, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 4, "query": "At the outset of group counseling, the therapist should explain char the obligation of the group member to respect confidentiality is\n\nA. on the “honor system” only\nB. protected by state/provincial laws\nC. less of an issue than it is in individual therapy\nD. mandated by federal law\nE. the legal responsibility of the therapist\nF. only applicable to the therapist\nG. only necessary if sensitive information is shared\nH. dependent on the group's consensus\nI. not applicable in group settings\n\nAnswer with the correct option letter and its content.", "input_path": "/data/audio_pool/q0175.wav", "input_sha256": "fa5307afe910cd5a70f553f4778be5ff4ea9f094ac909086fecdea4e2950b2ed", "input_samples": 541800, "input_s": 33.862, "n_real_chunks": 34, "score": 0.4589, "act": 0.9998, "is_info": true, "fired": false, "mode": "local", "answer": "The correct answer is E. Con fidentiality in group counseling is the legal responsibility of the therapist, and it must be clearly explained to ensure all participants understand their obligation s.", "relay_text": "", "expert_answer": "", "transcript": "", "asr_s": null, "expert_s": null, "expert_input_samples": null, "expert_input_s": null, "expert_input_sha256": null, "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": null, "relay_synth_ms": null, "onset_chunk": 33, "eot_seen": true, "n_speak_chunks": 11, "feed_lag_max_ms": 0, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 0, "audio_files": {"local": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0175_local_local.wav", "sha256": "0a40c31b4c37dd43e4ae1dd7186d3df973d2dbb78b61e81b2dd11d9f1dffbe94", "sr": 24000, "seco